One important thing for EKS

Your backend pods inside EKS usually won’t automatically use app_sg.

They typically use:

EKS node security group

or pod ENI SG.

So later RDS may fail with:

connection refused

because DB allows:

app_sg

but EKS nodes use another SG.

Best option

Allow both:

Change DB ingress to:

resource "aws_security_group" "db_sg" {
  name   = "db-sg"
  vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id

  ingress {
    from_port       = 5432
    to_port         = 5432
    protocol        = "tcp"

    security_groups = [
      aws_security_group.app_sg.id
    ]
  }

  egress {
    from_port   = 0
    to_port     = 0
    protocol    = "-1"
    cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"]
  }
}

Then after Terraform apply, once EKS node SG is visible, add it too.

For now your current config is okay.

